<<<
ther. Confusion between this & together is not uncommon (Until at last, gathered altogether again, they find their way down to the turf./A long pull, a s pull, & a pull altogether./Great efforts have been made ...to bring the troops out altogether tn brigades, & even in divisions. All together should have been used in each). Altogether is right only in the senses entirely or on the whole.
===
**altogether.** Confusion between this & *all together* is not uncommon (*Until at last, gathered altogether again, they find their way down to the turf.*/*A long pull, a strong pull, & a pull altogether.*/*Great efforts have been made . . . to bring the troops out altogether in brigades, & even in divisions.* *All together* should have been used in each). *Altogether* is right only in the senses *entirely* or *on the whole*.
>>>

