<<<
America(n). The use of America for the United States & American for (citizen) of the U.S. is open to as much & as little objection as that of England & English(man) for Great Britain (& TIreland), British, & Briton. It will continue to be protested against by purists & patriots, & will doubtless survive the protests.
===
**America(n).** The use of *America* for *the United States & American* for (*citizen*) *of the U.S.* is open to as much & as little objection as that of *England & English(man)* for *Great Britain* (& *Ireland*), *British, & Briton*. It will continue to be protested against by purists & patriots, & will doubtless survive the protests.
>>>

